  "chapterId": "puc1-physics-04-laws-of-motion",
  "topicId": "puc1-physics-04-laws-of-motion.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A machine gun fires 240 bullets per minute, each of mass 10 g, with a speed of 600 m/s. The average force needed to hold the gun steady is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "240 N"
   },
   {
    "en": "24 N"
   },
   {
    "en": "2.4 N"
   },
   {
    "en": "144 N"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "240 per minute = 4 per second. F = (number per second) × mv = 4 × 0.01 × 600 = 24 N."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC",
   "KCET",
   "COMEDK",
   "NEET",
